Bimolecular recombination dynamics study.
We next focused on bimolecular recombination dynamics on the microsecond time scale. The charge carrier density $(n)$ and the charge carrier lifetime $\left(\tau_{n}\right)$ were evaluated by transient photovoltage (TPV) and transient photocurrent (TPC) measurements of the solar cells based on these polymers.43,44 Figure 10a displays the dependence of the small perturbation lifetime $\left(\tau_{\Delta n}\right)$ on $V_{\mathrm{OC}}$ obtained from the TPV measurement under different bias light intensities (from ${\sim}0.1$ to 1.0 sun). In all cases, $\tau_{\Delta n}$ decreased exponentially with increasing $V_{\mathrm{OC}}$ , and hence was fitted by $\tau_{\Delta n}=\tau_{\Delta n0}\exp(-\beta V_{\mathrm{OC}})$ with parameter $\beta=17$ , 19, and $22{\mathrm{~V}}^{-1}$ for the PNTz4T, PNTz4TF2, and PNTz4TF4 systems, respectively. Figure 10b displays the dependence of $n$ on $V_{\mathrm{OC}}$ obtained from the TPC measurement under different bias light intensities (from ${\sim}0.1$ to $1.0\ \mathrm{sun}\rangle$ . As shown in the figure, charge carrier density $n$ increased exponentially with increasing $V_{\mathrm{OC}}.$ , which was fitted by $n=n_{0}\mathbf{exp}(\gamma V_{\mathrm{OC}})$ with parameter $\gamma=9.1$ , 14, and $10~\mathrm{V}^{-1}$ for the PNTz4T, PNTz4TF2, and PNTz4TF4 systems, respectively. The charge carrier density $n$ at 1 sun was thus estimated to be $2.1\times10^{16}$ $(\mathrm{PNTz4T/PC_{71}B M})$ , $1.6\times10^{16}$ (PNTz4TF2/PC71BM), and $1.9\times10^{16}$ $\mathrm{cm}^{-3}$ $^3\mathrm{(PNTz4TF4/PC_{71}B M)}$ . As reported previously,43,44 the charge carrier lifetime $\tau_{n}$ is given by $\tau_{n}=(1$ $+\lambda)\tau_{\Delta n}$ with $\lambda=\beta/\gamma$ . Consequently, as shown in Figure 10c, the carrier-density dependence of $\tau_{n}$ is well described by a power law equation $(\tau_{n}=\tau_{0}n^{-\lambda})$ . Thus, $\tau_{n}$ at 1 sun was estimated to be 6.3, 3.0, and $5.6~\upmu\mathrm{s}$ for the PNTz4T, PNTz4TF2, and PNTz4TF4 systems, respectively.
On the basis of the TPV/TPC measurements, the effective bimolecular recombination coefficient $\left(k_{\mathrm{rec}}\right)$ is given by $k_{\mathrm{rec}}=1/n\tau_{n}$ .43-45 Under the 1 sun illumination condition, as summarized in Table 5, $k_{\mathrm{rec}}$ is $7.5\times10^{-12}\mathrm{cm}^{3}\mathrm{s}^{-1}$ for the PNTz4T system, which is smaller than $2.1\times10^{-11}$ and $9.3\times10^{-12}\mathrm{cm}^{3}\mathrm{s}^{-1}$ estimated for the PNTz4TF2 and the PNTz4TF4 cells, respectively. On the other hand, the Langevin recombination rate is given by $k_{\mathrm{L}}=q\mu/\varepsilon_{0}\varepsilon$ , where $q$ is the elementary charge, $\mu$ is the slower charge carrier mobility, $^{46}\ \varepsilon_{0}$ is the vacuum permittivity, and $\varepsilon$ is the dielectric constant. Here, $\mu$ was evaluated by the SCLC method and $\varepsilon$ was assumed to be 3.5. Thus, $k_{\mathrm{L}}\mathrm{s}$ were calculated to be $5.8\times10^{-10}$ , $7.9\times$ ${{10}^{-10}}$ , and $9.4\times10^{-11}~\mathrm{{cm}^{3}~\mathrm{{s}^{-1}}}$ for the PNTz4T, PNTz4TF2, and PNTz4TF4 systems, respectively, as
