## Conclusion
We have synthesized two novel NTz-based polymers with fluorinated bithiophene units, namely, PNTz4TF2 and PNTz4TF4. The fluorination preferentially stabilized the HOMO of the polymers, resulting in larger $E_{\mathrm{H}}\mathbf{s}$ , slightly larger $E_{\mathrm{{L}}}\mathrm{{s}}$ , and slightly wider $E_{\mathrm{g}}\mathbf{s}$ for PNTz4TF2 and PNTz4TF4 relative to a non-fluorinated polymer, PNTz4T. As expected from the deep $E_{\mathrm{H}}\mathbf{s}$ , $V_{\mathrm{OCS}}$ of the PNTz4TF2 and PNTz4TF4 cells were improved to $0.82\mathrm{~V~}$ and $0.93{\mathrm{~V~}}$ , respectively, relative to that of the PNTz4T cell (0.71 V). As a result, the $E_{\mathrm{loss}}\mathrm{\bfS}$ of the PNTz4TF2 and PNTz4TF4 cells were reduced to $0.78\mathrm{eV}$ and 0.69 eV, respectively, from that of the PNTz4T cell (0.82 eV). Compared with the PNTz4T cell, the PNTz4TF4 cell exhibited ${\sim}6.5\%$ PCE and lower $J_{\mathrm{SC}}$ and FF, whereas the PNTz4TF2 cell had ${\sim}10.5\%$ PCE with similar $J_{\mathrm{SC}}$ and lower FF. The PCE of the PNTz4TF2 cell is higher than that of the PNTz4T cell $(\sim10.1\%)$ and is significantly high for single-junction PSCs. The charge generation study revealed that charge dissociation is the dominant factor for the difference in $J_{\mathrm{SC}}$ among these cells. The bimolecular recombination study demonstrated that recombination was increased as the number of fluorine atoms was increased, and this was likely the cause of the lower FF of the PNTz4TF2 and PNTz4TF4 cells than the PNTz4T cell. These behaviors were well correlated with the difference in crystallinity and backbone orientation investigated by 2D GIXD measurements: crystallinity was low particularly in PNTz4TF4, and the ratio of the face-on orientation was reduced in PNTz4TF2 and PNTz4TF4 compared to that in PNTz4T. However, it should be mentioned that the poor ordering structures in the fluorinated polymers likely originate in their low solubility, probably owing to the enhanced backbone coplanarity as predicted by the computation. Thus, we believe that by tuning the solubility and optimizing the fabrication process, the photovoltaic performance of the solar cells based on PNTz4TF2 and PNTz4TF4 would be further increased. These results demonstrate that there is still room for improvement of the efficiency of PSCs.
